    rdfs:comment "TOPOGRAPHIC PLACEs which are adjacent to the TOPOGRAPHIC PLACE. or which partially overlay. N.B. this should not be used for spatial containment. Instead the Parent Site should be used the TOPOGRAPHIC PLACE which completely contain the TOPOGRAPHIC PLACE, and on child TOPOGRAPHIC PLACEs for localities completely contained in the TOPOGRAPHIC PLACE."@en ;
    rdfs:domain netex:TopographicPlace ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://vocabulary.eona-x.eu/ontology/netex/v1.0.0#> ;
